// 02 · Divide — trophic dependence, shown in a single frame.
//
// The arena is split by an impassable DIAGONAL wall of rocks (`Source { solid: true }`, a
// static collider each — impassable to bodies AND to seed-dispersal — running corner to
// corner). The SAME grazer runs in the two triangular halves on DIFFERENT ground:
//   • UPPER-LEFT — nutrient vents feed a stand of PRODUCERS (sessile photosynthesisers), and
//     grazers graze them: energy (and the nutrient it carries) flows up the chain, so the
//     herd PERSISTS and oscillates with its food (Lotka-Volterra).
//   • LOWER-RIGHT — the same grazers, but NO producers and no vents: nothing to eat. They pay
//     the allometric cost law every second (SIM Law 1/7) and, finding no energy, drift, thin,
//     and wink out — the bare "price of being alive" (the retired 01_drift lesson), now the
//     control half of a living comparison.
//
// One frame therefore carries the whole point: a consumer is not self-sufficient — strip its
// producers and it dies, however capable it is. The field leaks a little nutrient across the
// wall, but it is inert here: the bare side has no producer to absorb it and the grazers feed
// only by eating, so the lower-right herd starves regardless.
//
// Watch: the upper-left half stays green-and-orange and breathing; the lower-right goes quiet.
(
    tick_hz: 64.0,
    arena_half_extent: 440.0,
    archetypes: [
        (
            // Fed grazer — confined to the UPPER-LEFT half, where the producers grow.
            name: "Grazer (fed)",
            color: (1.0, 0.55, 0.35),
            count: 8,
            radius: 8.0,
            reserve_max: 120.0,
            genotype: (
                max_speed: 100.0,
                agility: 0.12,
                vision_range: 110.0,
                vision_fov_deg: 130.0,
                reproduction_threshold: 100.0,
                offspring_energy: 45.0,
                mutation_rate: 0.06,
                vision_rays: 7.0,
                seed_dispersal: 15.0,
            ),
            brain: Hunter,
            mutable: (mutation_rate: false),
            spawn_zone: Some((shape: Circle(center: (-147.0, 147.0), radius: 180.0))),
        ),
        (
            // Starved grazer — identical body, confined to the LOWER-RIGHT half, where there
            // is nothing to eat.
            name: "Grazer (starved)",
            color: (0.62, 0.4, 0.42),
            count: 8,
            radius: 8.0,
            reserve_max: 120.0,
            genotype: (
